This is documentation for the matlab file Floating_ice_sheets.m


MISC NOTES
- The functions are defined without an END statement
- par.S_filename is defined in set_parameters, modify path/to/file to avoid errors when running S_total
- Optimization Toolbox is required to run code

FUNCTIONS

set_parameters
---------------------
input: .m file
output: returns an object par
Takes as input the experiment number which is a file where the following params are defined:
	par.model_to_run='2d-sphere';
	par.linearized_model=0;
	par.T_surface_profile_type='warm';
Defines all param of the modeled object.
Applies land mask if applicable and tests consistency.
Defines the limits of the physical domain and converts everything in spherical coords.



read_restart
---------------------
input: par object, which_restart: 
	'goodman', 'goodman-linear', '1d-nonlinear', '1d-linear', '2d-sphere-linear', '2d-sphere-nonlinear'
output: params
Checks if there is a restart file to loop through the scenario multiple times and use the output param of the previous run as the input param of the next one.
Sets the previous params as current param if a restart file has been created.


